'' T58, RUN: a name declared anywhere on the scope chain -- the module, an enclosing
'' namespace -- beats a 'using' written in a sub, a scope or a namespace, as fbc rules;
'' the using answers only when the chain has nothing. tiko took the nearer using first.
'' Output identical to fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/using-precedence.bas -o tests/codegen/usingprec.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/usingprec.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: sub: 1 10 100
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: scope: 1 10 100
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: M: 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: only: 1
